### Basic health check
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health

### Full health check
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health?full=true

### Check specific service
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health?service=database

### Check with custom timeout
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health?timeout=10000

### Test error handling (404 Not Found)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/not-exist 

### Test Service Error
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health/test-error?type=SERVICE

### Test Validation Error
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health/test-error?type=VALIDATION

### Test Database Error
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health/test-error?type=DATABASE

### Test Uncaught Error
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health/test-error?type=UNCAUGHT

### Test Unknown Error
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health/test-error?type=unknown 

### Process Management Tests ###

# 1. Start the server with:
# npm run dev
#
# 2. Test graceful shutdown with different signals:
#    a. SIGTERM: kill -15 <PID>
#    b. SIGINT: Press Ctrl+C in terminal
#    c. SIGUSR2: kill -12 <PID>
#
# 3. Check logs for:
#    - Shutdown signal received
#    - Resource cleanup
#    - Server close
#    - Process exit
#
# 4. Verify database connections:
#    - Run health check before shutdown
#    - Try to make requests during shutdown
#    - Check database state after restart
#
# Expected Results:
# - All signals should trigger graceful shutdown
# - Resources should be cleaned up properly
# - No hanging connections
# - Logs should show proper shutdown sequence

### GraphQL User API Tests ###

### Query - Get All Users
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { users { id email name createdAt updatedAt } }"
}

### Query - Get User by ID
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($id: Int!) { user(id: $id) { id email name createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": 1
  }
}

### Mutation - Create User
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($input: CreateUserInput!) { createUser(input: $input) { id email name createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": {
    "input": {
      "email": "test@example.com",
      "name": "Test User"
    }
  }
}

### Mutation - Create User with Invalid Email
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($input: CreateUserInput!) { createUser(input: $input) { id email name } }",
  "variables": {
    "input": {
      "email": "invalid-email",
      "name": "Test User"
    }
  }
}

### Mutation - Update User
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($id: Int!, $input: UpdateUserInput!) { updateUser(id: $id, input: $input) { id email name } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": 1,
    "input": {
      "name": "Updated Name"
    }
  }
}

### Mutation - Delete User
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($id: Int!) { deleteUser(id: $id) }",
  "variables": {
    "id": 1
  }
}